<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Makran State</h1><p class="st-meta">1898 CE – 1955 CE (approx.) · capital Turbat</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A coastal Baloch principality under the Khanate of Kalat, ruled by Gichki Nawabs from Turbat, which joined Pakistan in 1948.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Makran, the arid coastal region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a>, was under the overlordship of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kalat">Khanate of Kalat</a>, while local power lay with the Gichki family. By the end of the 19th century the Gichki Nawabs ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kech-district">Kech</a>-Makran as a dependency of Kalat.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state was thinly populated, with date palms in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kech-district">Kech</a> valley, fishing on the coast and trade through ports such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pasni">Pasni</a>. The Nawabs ruled with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kalat">Kalat</a> and British political officers looking on. The port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gwadar">Gwadar</a> on its coast belonged to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a> until 1958.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In March 1948 Makran acceded to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-republic-of-pakistan">Pakistan</a> independently of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kalat">Kalat</a>. It joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/baluchistan-states-union">Baluchistan States Union</a> in 1952 and was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-pakistan">West Pakistan</a> in 1955; it is now a division of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/makran-state.jpg" alt="Makran State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: EuropeanV · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Makran_(Princely_State).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1898 CE – 1955 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Turbat</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam; Zikri Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Balochi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kech-Makran, Makran</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1926&amp;focus=makran-state" aria-label="Makran State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6346 1222 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Makran State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6666 1478L6738 1372M6666 1478L7364 1602M6666 1478L6778 1519M6666 1478L6738 1372"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6738 1372h0M7364 1602h0M6778 1519h0M6738 1372h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6666 1478h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6666 1478h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Turbat. <a href="/atlas?year=1926&amp;focus=makran-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
